node_modules/
dist/
# Every env variant, not just .env — this repo holds the database URL, the
# JWT secret and the Cloudinary credentials, so a stray .env.production here
# is the worst of the four to leak. The example stays committed on purpose:
# it documents what to set and carries only placeholders.
.env*
!.env.example
prisma/dev.db
prisma/dev.db-journal
*.log

# Locally uploaded user content, written by StorageService when no Cloudinary
# credentials are set. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: a bare
# `uploads/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently
# swallowed src/uploads/ — five source files that built locally and were simply
# absent on the build machine.
/uploads/

# Vercel
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
